    "statement": "There is insufficient research directly comparing the effectiveness of restoring degraded coastal habitats versus creating new artificial habitats specifically for seal population conservation.",
    "citations": []
  },
  {
    "statement": "Habitat restoration efforts for coastal wetlands show positive results for bird species use.",
    "citations": [
      "367"
    ]
  },
  {
    "statement": "Legal habitat protection has demonstrated benefits for marine mammal populations, including Mediterranean monk seals.",
    "citations": [
      "2915"
    ]
  },
  {
    "statement": "There are no studies found that directly evaluate creating artificial habitats for marine mammals.",
    "citations": [
      "2921"
    ]
  },
  {
    "statement": "There are no studies evaluating the effects on marine mammal populations of leaving anthropogenic structures in place after decommissioning.",
    "citations": [
      "2922"
    ]
  },
  {
    "statement": "The evidence base for offsetting habitat loss through restoration or creation elsewhere is limited to invertebrate species.",
    "citations": [
      "2265"
    ]
  },
  {
    "statement": "A lack of comparative research means conclusions cannot be drawn about which approach would be more effective for seal conservation.",
    "citations": []
  }
